{
  "$comment": "Inputs of deno-notices.mjs, which writes licenses/deno/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt: the notices of the third-party code built into the Deno program Mergelane ships (ADR-0029). Every URL is pinned to a commit or checked against a SHA-256. Deno's release publishes no such list (checked 2026-11-11: the v2.9.8 release assets, the repository at the tag, and `deno --help`). The V8 components are rusty_v8's submodules at the commit the v8 crate in Deno's Cargo.lock was published from (its .cargo_vcs_info.json), minus the ones used only to build (build, buildtools, tools/clang, tools/win, third_party/jinja2, third_party/markupsafe, third_party/rust, V8's third_party/colorama). docs/MEDIA-TOOLS.md says how to update this file. crateFallbacks: for each crate whose package has no licence file of its own (122 of 1048 on 2026-11-11), the licence files of its repository at the commit in its .cargo_vcs_info.json (in the crate's own folder, else the repository's top level), found with GitHub's contents API; for the swc crates, whose recorded commits are not in swc's repository, swc's LICENSE at a pinned commit. spdxTexts: for the crates left (no repository or commit, or no licence file there), the standard texts of the licences they declare, from SPDX's license-list-data v3.29.0.",
